SoftISP: lengthen the sensor frame in low light (libcamera 0.8.0)

Applied by build-patched-libcamera.sh step 4d, on libcamera 0.8.0 full
installs only. Off unless the tuning file sets Agc maxFrameDuration (us).

With it set, the SoftISP AGC may expose for longer than the default frame
allows: the IPA raises the AGC's exposure limit to maxFrameDuration minus the
sensor's exposure margin, and sends V4L2_CID_VBLANK with each exposure so the
frame is only lengthened as far as that exposure needs. The simple pipeline
writes VBLANK before exposure and gain (DelayedControls priority write, or a
separate write first when there is no frame start event).

libipa's AgcAlgorithm already handles FrameDurationLimits and computes a
VBLANK, but in 0.8.0 the SoftISP never sends it and its exposure limit stays
at the default frame length ("\todo take VBLANK into account for maximum
exposure time").

It also reports the frame length each frame had as FrameDuration metadata.

